<code>assert \result != -1 => (\forall int i; i > \result && i < this.size(); (o == null && this.get(i) == null) || (o != null && !o.equals(this.get(i))));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \result != -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i < this.size(); (\old(o) == null) => this.get(i) == null || (\old(o) != null) => !\old(o).equals(this.get(i)));</code>

This assert statement captures the specification that if the result of `lastIndexOf` is not `-1`, then for every index `i` greater than the result and less than the size of the list, the element at that index is either `null` if the searched object is `null`, or not equal to the searched object if the searched object is not `null`.
--------------------
<code>assert \result != -1 => \forall int i; i > \result && i < this.size(); (o == null) ? this.get(i) == null : !o.equals(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
